# Obsidian local workplace states & caches
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspace*
.obsidian/cache/
.obsidian/indexed*
.obsidian/graph.json
# 🔌 Obsidian plugin runtime configuration (local-only, may hold secrets/state)
# Distributable plugin code (main.js, manifest.json, styles.css) stays tracked.
# Sanitized example defaults stay trackable (none ship today):
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/cache.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/reference-files/
!.obsidian/plugins/*/data.example.json
.trash/

# 🤖 Local AI Indices & Plugin Caches
.smart-env/
.claudian/

# 🛠️ Agent & Tool Runtime (local-only, never commit)
.omo/
.opencode/
.codegraph/
.opencode/node_modules/
.clinerules/

# 🧭 Local-only engineering layer — never published (owner decision 2026-10-04)
#
# This repository is the product for PKM users. The engineering control plane and
# the vault's own development history stay on the owner's machine. PromptKit OS
# ships from its own upstream repo (lowqualityloey/promptkit-os); vendoring it
# here would make every public clone fetch a second repository for zero
# consumer value, and the session/spec/task records are internal process, not
# documentation a user needs.
#
# These rules are STRUCTURAL, not advisory. Deletion does not remove content from
# git history, so the boundary has to hold before the commit rather than after
# it — the same reasoning as the PERSONAL CONTENT block further down.
#
# Tracked on the local-only branch chore/promptkit-engine-and-state, never merged.
.promptkit/
PROMPTKIT.md
docs/
GEMINI.md
#
# ⚠️  AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md ARE tracked, so ignore rules cannot protect them.
#    The PromptKit directive block appended to them lives only on the local
#    branch — strip it before opening any PR that touches either file.

# GitButler state lives in .git/ (never tracked by definition) — belt-and-suspenders:
.git/gitbutler/
.git/butler/

# 🔒 SECRETS & SENSITIVE KEYS (NEVER COMMIT TO GIT)
.secrets/
00-Private/
*.env
*.env.*
*_secret*
*_private*
!.env.example

# System & sync files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.directory
.tmp.*
*.tmp
.tmp.driveupload/
.tmp.drivedownload/
*.sync-conflict-*

# IDE & Editor configurations
.vscode/
.idea/

# Node & TypeScript Build artifacts
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
06-Resources/scripts/dist/
.enriched-timestamps.json

# Logs & temp
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# 📓 PERSONAL CONTENT (the system is shareable, the journal is not)
# History audit found 8 daily notes had been committed and later deleted —
# deletion does not remove them from history, so these rules make the boundary
# structural instead of relying on never typing `git add -A`.
# MOCs and already-tracked showcase files stay tracked; everything else is isolated.

00-Inbox/*
!00-Inbox/_*.md

01-Daily/*
!01-Daily/_*.md

02-Projects/*
!02-Projects/_*.md

03-Dev/*
!03-Dev/_*.md

04-Learning/*
!04-Learning/_*.md

05-Personal/*
!05-Personal/_*.md

06-Resources/Articles/*
!06-Resources/Articles/_*.md

07-Reviews/*
!07-Reviews/_*.md
!07-Reviews/Habit Analytics Dashboard.md

08-Concepts/*
!08-Concepts/_*.md

99-Attachments/*
!99-Attachments/_*.md
!99-Attachments/2026-08/obsidian-*.png
!99-Attachments/2026-08/file-20260803003355764.png

